    <header class="bg-gradient-to-r from-sunYellow to-sunOrange text-white py-8 px-6 text-center">
        <h1 class="font-heading text-[clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3rem)] font-bold text-shadow-sm mb-2">
            ☀️ The Sun’s Influence on Earth
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg opacity-95">Understanding how the Sun shapes life, weather, and energy on our planet</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Navigation Tabs -->
    <nav class="bg-deepBlue text-white px-4 sticky top-0 z-40 shadow-md">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto flex flex-wrap justify-center">
            <a href="#life" class="tab-link px-6 py-3 hover:bg-sunYellow/80 hover:text-black transition">Life</a>
            <a href="#weather" class="tab-link px-6 py-3 hover:bg-sunYellow/80 hover:text-black transition">Weather</a>
            <a href="#seasons" class="tab-link px-6 py-3 hover:bg-sunYellow/80 hover:text-black transition">Seasons</a>
            <a href="#energy" class="tab-link px-6 py-3 hover:bg-sunYellow/80 hover:text-black transition">Energy</a>
            <a href="#activities" class="tab-link px-6 py-3 hover:bg-sunYellow/80 hover:text-black transition">Activities</a>
            <a href="#quiz" class="tab-link px-6 py-3 hover:bg-sunYellow/80 hover:text-black transition">Quiz</a>
            <a href="#references" class="tab-link px-6 py-3 hover:bg-sunYellow/80 hover:text-black transition">References</a>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Learning Objectives -->
    <section class="py-10 px-6 bg-white/70 border-b border-sunYellow/20" id="objectives">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h3 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold text-deepBlue mb-4">🎯 Learning Objectives</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-lg">
                <li>Explain how the Sun provides energy for all living things through photosynthesis</li>
                <li>Describe how uneven heating causes weather patterns, wind, and ocean currents</li>
                <li>Relate Earth’s tilt and orbit to the changing seasons</li>
                <li>Identify the benefits of solar energy as a renewable resource</li>
                <li>Connect the Sun’s influence to real-life phenomena and daily life</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 1: LIFE -->
    <section class="py-14 px-6" id="life">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md p-8 card-hover border-l-4 border-green-600">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
                    <i class="fa fa-leaf text-2xl text-green-600"></i>
                    <h2 class="font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-bold text-green-700">The Sun and Life on Earth</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    The Sun is the **primary source of energy** for all living things on Earth. Without sunlight, life as we know it would not exist.
                </p>

                <div class="bg-green-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-5">
                    <p class="font-medium">🌿 <strong>Photosynthesis Process:</strong><br>
                    Green plants, algae, and some bacteria use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make food (glucose). This process releases oxygen — the gas humans and animals breathe.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p class="text-lg">
                    Every food chain starts with plants. Herbivores eat plants; carnivores eat herbivores. Ultimately, <em>all energy comes from the Sun</em>.
                </p>

                <!-- Activity Snippet -->
                <div class="mt-6 p-4 bg-green-50/50 rounded-lg border border-green-100">
                    <strong>💡 Think:</strong> What would happen to plants if the Sun disappeared? How would it affect you?
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 2: WEATHER -->
    <section class="py-14 px-6 bg-deepBlue/5" id="weather">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md p-8 card-hover border-l-4 border-skyBlue">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
                    <i class="fa fa-cloud text-2xl text-skyBlue"></i>
                    <h2 class="font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-bold text-skyBlue">The Sun and Weather</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    The Sun does not heat the Earth evenly. It warms areas near the equator more strongly than areas near the poles. This **uneven heating** is the engine of all weather.
                </p>

                <ul class="space-y-3 mb-5 text-lg">
                    <li>🌬️ <strong>Wind:</strong> Warm air rises; cool air rushes in to replace it → creates wind.</li>
                    <li>🌧️ <strong>Rain & Clouds:</strong> Sun evaporates water from oceans/lakes → forms clouds → falls as rain/snow.</li>
                    <li>🌊 <strong>Ocean Currents:</strong> Warm water moves from equator toward poles; cold water flows back → regulates global temperature.</li>
                    <li>⛈️ <strong>Storms:</strong> Differences in heat and pressure create storms, typhoons, and monsoons.</li>
                </ul>

                <p class="italic text-gray-600">
                    *Simply put: The Sun drives the water cycle and air movement.*
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 3: SEASONS -->
    <section class="py-14 px-6" id="seasons">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md p-8 card-hover border-l-4 border-amber-600">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
                    <i class="fa fa-globe text-2xl text-amber-600"></i>
                    <h2 class="font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-bold text-amber-700">The Sun and Seasons</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    Seasons are NOT caused by how close Earth is to the Sun — they are caused by **Earth’s 23.5° tilt** and its yearly orbit around the Sun.
                </p>

                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
                    <div class="p-4 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg">
                        <strong>☀️ Summer:</strong> Earth’s axis tilts *toward* the Sun. Sunlight hits directly → more heat, longer days.
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg">
                        <strong>❄️ Winter:</strong> Earth’s axis tilts *away* from the Sun. Sunlight hits at a slant → less heat, shorter days.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <p class="text-lg">
                    Spring and Autumn happen when Earth is moving between these two positions.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SECTION 4: ENERGY -->
    <section class="py-14 px-6 bg-green-50/30" id="energy">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md p-8 card-hover border-l-4 border-yellow-500">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
                    <i class="fa fa-bolt text-2xl text-yellow-500"></i>
                    <h2 class="font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-bold text-yellow-600">Solar Energy</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    The Sun provides an endless supply of clean, renewable energy — the most abundant energy source on Earth.
                </p>

                <ul class="space-y-3 mb-5 text-lg">
                    <li>✅ <strong>Renewable:</strong> Never runs out (for billions of years).</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Clean:</strong> No smoke, no pollution, no carbon dioxide.</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Uses:</strong> Solar panels turn sunlight into electricity; solar heaters warm water; greenhouses grow food year-round.</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Benefit:</strong> Helps fight climate change and reduces reliance on fossil fuels.</li>
                </ul>

                <div class="bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
                    <p class="font-medium">💡 Did you know? The Sun sends enough energy to Earth in <em>one hour</em> to power the whole world for <em>one year</em>!</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- LEARNING ACTIVITIES (Pedagogy / Constructivist / Dale's Cone) -->
    <section class="py-14 px-6 bg-deepBlue/10" id="activities">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-bold text-center text-deepBlue mb-10">📝 Learning Activities</h2>
            
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                <!-- Activity 1 -->
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-md">
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-sunOrange mb-3">🔎 Activity 1 – Observe & Record</h4>
                    <p><strong>Level:</strong> Direct Experience (Dale’s Cone)<br>
                    Track your shadow at 9AM, 12PM, and 3PM. How does length/direction change? Relate it to Sun’s position.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Activity 2 -->
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-md">
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-sunOrange mb-3">🌬️ Activity 2 – Explain the Wind</h4>
                    <p><strong>Level:</strong> Symbolic / Analysis<br>
                    Write 3 sentences: How does the Sun cause wind? Use the words: <em>heat, rise, cool, move</em>.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Activity 3 -->
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-md md:col-span-2">
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-sunOrange mb-3">⚗️ Activity 3 – Experiment: Solar Heat</h4>
                    <p><strong>Level:</strong> Contrived Experience<br>
                    Place two thermometers: one in sunlight, one in shade. Record temperature every 10 minutes for 1 hour. Graph the results.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- QUIZ / ASSESSMENT -->
    <section class="py-14 px-6" id="quiz">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-bold text-center text-deepBlue mb-8">✔️ Check Your Understanding</h2>
            
            <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md p-8">
                <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-lg mb-8">
                    <li>How does the Sun help plants make food?</li>
                    <li>Why do different places on Earth have different temperatures?</li>
                    <li>What two things cause the seasons?</li>
                    <li>Name three ways humans use energy from the Sun.</li>
                    <li>Why is solar energy better than coal or oil?</li>
                </ol>

                <details class="bg-lightCream p-4 rounded-lg border border-sunYellow/30">
                    <summary class="font-bold text-sunOrange cursor-pointer">📌 See Answer Key</summary>
                    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
                        <li>1. Through photosynthesis: sunlight + water + CO₂ → food + oxygen</li>
                        <li>2. Uneven heating — more heat at equator, less at poles</li>
                        <li>3. Earth’s tilt (23.5°) + orbit/revolution around the Sun</li>
                        <li>4. Electricity (panels), heat, growing food, drying clothes</li>
                        <li>5. Clean, renewable, no pollution, unlimited supply</li>
                    </ul>
                </details>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

